Chapter: CharAtNegative
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A negative index must trap. Before the guard it read BACKWARDS out of the
 text and answered whatever lay before it.

 This is the first of the two char-index guards. The other is index past the
 end, in codex/test/char-at-past-end.codex; they fail for different reasons
 and neither can stand in for the other, which is why they are two files.

 `.fatal`: this dies on UD2, so there is no output to compare and -Fatal is
 not part of a routine battery. The battery-visible half is
 codex/test/ops/char-at-bounds.codex.

Section: Entry

  s : Text = "abcde"

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("got=" & show (char-code-at s (0 - 1)))
  end

